  "executive_summary": "## Q1 Retail Media Recommendation\n\nWe recommend an allocation of $10.0M across 5 retailers. This reallocation is grounded in our Bayesian elasticity analysis: In Store Display shows the highest elasticity of 0.43 (90% CI: 0.37-0.50).\n\n**Expected Outcomes:**\n- Incremental Sales: $4.4M (90% CI: $4.2M - $4.6M)\n- ROAS: 0.4x\n- Stockout Risk: 19.5%\n",
  "detailed_rationale": "### Scenario Analysis\n\n**Baseline**: $4.3M expected sales, 0.4x ROAS, 15.0% stockout risk\n**High Elasticity**: $4.3M expected sales, 0.4x ROAS, 15.0% stockout risk\n**Inventory Safe**: $4.3M expected sales, 0.4x ROAS, 15.0% stockout risk\n**Explore Uncertain**: $4.3M expected sales, 0.4x ROAS, 15.0% stockout risk\n**Demand Surge**: $4.4M expected sales, 0.4x ROAS, 19.5% stockout risk\n**Supply Disruption**: $3.5M expected sales, 0.4x ROAS, 19.2% stockout risk\n\n### Retailer Allocation\n\n- **walmart**: $2.00M (20% of budget)\n- **kroger**: $2.00M (20% of budget)\n- **target**: $2.00M (20% of budget)\n- **costco**: $2.00M (20% of budget)\n- **albertsons**: $2.00M (20% of budget)\n",
  "uncertainty_acknowledgment": "### Key Uncertainties\n\nOur sponsored search elasticity estimate for walmart has high variance (coefficient of variation: 21%) due to limited measurement data. \n\nThe 90% credible interval on expected sales spans $4.2M to $4.6M, reflecting simulation uncertainty across 1000 Monte Carlo paths.\n\n**Binding Constraints**: inventory_capacity, inventory:walmart, inventory:kroger, inventory:target, inventory:costco, inventory:albertsons",
